      "content": "Here is a punchier alternative that emphasizes the ideological \"blindfold.\"\n\n\"Far from being a simple political endorsement, *The Stone Orchard* operates as a devastating critique of ideological certainty, using the partisan faction as a primary site for this argument. The powerful political beliefs of the opposing side are ultimately shown to function less as conviction and more as a self-imposed cognitive defense mechanism. These rigid views act as a powerful, and ultimately limiting, blindfold, preventing the supporting cast from truly engaging with the nuanced reality of the world around them and the other side of the argument.",
      "source": "target",
